<div class="pitfall">A declared variable is shared by <strong>every user and every thread</strong> (Tomcat runs one object of the servlet for all requests, Chapter 2). Never keep per-user data in <code>&lt;%! %&gt;</code> — "the logged-in user", "the cart", "the search keyword" put there leak from one user to the next, and <code>++count</code> from two threads at once can lose updates. Per-request data → local variable or request attribute; per-user → session (Chapter 4).</div>
