<p>A <strong>MIME type</strong> (media type) is the label in the <code>Content-Type</code> header that tells the browser how to treat the body: <code>text/html</code>, <code>text/plain</code>, <code>application/json</code>, <code>image/gif</code>… The slide's page, unchanged (a 42-byte GIF in the app), requested with HEAD so that only the headers are shown:</p>
