<p>Here they stay in <code>out</code>'s buffer and are silently thrown away (the body is exactly 42 bytes); add one character of text before the scriptlet and you get the famous <code>IllegalStateException: getOutputStream() has already been called</code>. Three more problems: the stream is never closed (a file handle leaks on every request), it copies one byte per call, and — the real lesson — <strong>a JSP is the wrong tool for binary data</strong>. Tomcat serves the same file by itself:</p>
