<p>The URI was found (the old jar's TLD declares it), but its classes are built on <code>javax.servlet.jsp</code>, which Tomcat 10+ no longer has — "chỉ đổi tên gói" <code>javax</code> → <code>jakarta</code>, as the ⭐ "Start here" lesson explains, but an old jar cannot be renamed. 3 — The fallback URI: <code>…/jsp/jstl/core_rt</code> has never existed, in JSTL 1.1 or 3.0 (the real JSTL 1.0 "rt" URI has no <code>/jsp/</code>) — measured:</p>
